{"title":"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Trig)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Trig)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Heron&#39;s_Theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Heron's Theorem)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Stewart&#39;s_Theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Stewart's Theorem)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/f/7ff29028b2432b4e2cf3d924ac82114813de066d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=5$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/5/8e579aa3fd1791a4ac67ca281f43c5fffd9929eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=7$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c356cf0e82b342a8157ca8e2811447a5c25a639.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=9$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/1/bb1064b607676819b46b58a2a13b6f4aea9a22af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=5$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />. Find the ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a445944867a816c830c19a20ac99e734c34a753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD:DC$\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/e/85ef7a332d4265d8f052349a58f701f82e2d07aa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((3,4)--(0,0)--(9,0)--(3,4)--(6,0)); dot((0,0));dot((9,0));dot((3,4));dot((6,0)); label(&quot;A&quot;, (0,0), W); label(&quot;B&quot;, (3,4), N); label(&quot;C&quot;, (9,0), E); label(&quot;D&quot;, (6,0), S);[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"135\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/c/0ac002c5d0e5f6ff2802081fac5cf8e1dd1b1521.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textrm{(A)}\\ 4:3\\qquad\\textrm{(B)}\\ 7:5\\qquad\\textrm{(C)}\\ 11:6\\qquad\\textrm{(D)}\\ 13:5\\qquad\\textrm{(E)}\\ 19:8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"478\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/d/e5d60ae241b0cfde5d142e61e289305386313b26.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((3,4)--(0,0)--(9,0)--(3,4)--(6,0)); draw((3,4)--(3,0),dotted); dot((0,0));dot((9,0));dot((3,4));dot((6,0));//dot((3,0)); label(&quot;A&quot;, (0,0), W); label(&quot;B&quot;, (3,4), N); label(&quot;C&quot;, (9,0), E); label(&quot;D&quot;, (6,0), S); label(&quot;$h$&quot;, (3,1.5),W); draw(rightanglemark((3,1),(3,0),(4,0),10)); label(&quot;$x$&quot;,(1.5,0),S);label(&quot;$x$&quot;,(4.5,0),S); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"135\" />\nDrop the altitude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />. Then by Pythagoras <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/2/1f2b96de36cf9055c9f76b18f168b760805f193b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{cases}h^2+x^2=25\\\\h^2+(9-x)^2=49\\end{cases}\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"53\" /> and after subtracting the first equation from the second, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/6/346de33874a5a3d97337fdeb204fbe3aa8576a03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=3\\tfrac16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"52\" height=\"21\" />. Therefore the desired ratio is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/4/0142543b27824e55ee97d53ec92a27a6f18bde17.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{6\\tfrac13}{2\\tfrac23}=\\boxed{\\frac{19}8}\\]\" width=\"80\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Trig.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Trig)\">Solution 2 (Trig)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Trig)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using laws of cosines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3df79a4384bc29acd37e14b0430773d09964ddd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup ABC$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d1266d850892940f38c68e1778da8ba1815e81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49=25+81-2 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 9 \\cdot \\cos A \\implies \\cos A =\\frac{19}{30}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"375\" height=\"38\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/e/7beb1c45175e8a3bb4c3e6cd2f4624412dcf22ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=x.$\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" /> Using laws of cosines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/7/bf7c03416343b056378828e992f8b4ec4cf76925.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup ABD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5636b4e6740be295475288132bdc76a8402ad9f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25+x^2-2 \\cdot 5 \\cdot x \\cdot \\cos A = 25.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"235\" height=\"16\" /> Fortunately, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/2/4a264947b889477708795e4ce7dd11fc4be808d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos A =\\frac{19}{30}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"38\" /> Plugging this information back into our equation yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/f/33fbe168757620757d0547077fdd6e80c97bf8f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{19}{3}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"60\" height=\"37\" /> Then, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6a6a97a0b923a496a60c55ca65b24b896c6dfb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC=9-\\frac{19}{3}=\\frac{8}{3} \\implies\\frac{AD}{DC}=\\boxed{\\frac{19}{8}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"293\" height=\"49\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Heron.27s_Theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Heron's_Theorem)\">Solution 3 (Heron's Theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Heron&#39;s Theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By Heron's Theorem, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/d/38de283f80d61241215419257d9ce97e45c8b533.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac{21}{2} \\cdot \\frac{11}{2} \\cdot \\frac{7}{2} \\cdot \\frac{3}{2}} = \\frac{21\\sqrt{11}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"209\" height=\"45\" />.  \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/7/0177f243cbf12c582bcf38ed6a5ed9f8451be53a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h = BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/a/91ab0a2b5ad9a5c606efe68d29d5aa831d237d1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9h}{2} = \\frac{21\\sqrt{11}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"105\" height=\"43\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/5861da66f1e5ce917751282e8ad71e7d19244a5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h = \\frac{7\\sqrt{11}}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"83\" height=\"43\" />.  \n</p><p>By the Pythagorean theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/b/17b3998e2186d82cfe87ea40a26d3be60c922967.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = ED = \\sqrt{5^2 - \\left(\\frac{7\\sqrt{11}}{6}\\right)^2} = \\frac{19}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"294\" height=\"66\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/c/94cab9ec123da33e7f3985bef1c90ed36e95eb5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = \\frac{19}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"77\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/9/9a95d7c8a7e911803ca51fd68691ed65318acf02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC = 9 - \\frac{19}{3} = \\frac{8}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"147\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/3/863ebba163c21bb8d61024d604de3ab1f5e6583d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD : DC = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 19 : 8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"187\" height=\"30\" />.  \n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Stewart.27s_Theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Stewart's_Theorem)\">Solution 4 (Stewart's Theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Stewart&#39;s Theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/a/33ab3c8f2ad41073cfda7ce7e7305639821d3dd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = AD$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>By Stewart's Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/a/8da20dd1f0bc8920c3d254eb5e95ad606dfae65f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(BD)^2(AC) + (AC)(AD)(DC) = (AB)^2(CD) + (BC)^2(AD)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"482\" height=\"21\" />.  \n</p><p>Substituting yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/f/82f855375d45e05cae85588a805a4064f68755b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^2(9) + 9x(9-x) = 5^2 (9-x) +7^2(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"299\" height=\"21\" /> which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/f/6afb09181c2a74e90c6520df5f06d8bd78ea2d77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-9x^2 + 81x + 225 = 225 + 24x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"246\" height=\"18\" />.  Collecting all terms on one side yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/3/55387e73a965e181dfc255e7470959fe7e2022ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9x^2 - 57x = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" />, which factors as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/a/c5a669282e8a32bd1c0a73e5901fc1f8a8faacc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x(3x-19)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is positive, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/9/c59c3dae2709882a3e9a058fea32ae588d71fcf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{19}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/9/9a95d7c8a7e911803ca51fd68691ed65318acf02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC = 9 - \\frac{19}{3} = \\frac{8}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"147\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/3/863ebba163c21bb8d61024d604de3ab1f5e6583d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD : DC = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 19 : 8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"187\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME\" title=\"1989 AHSME\">1989 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1989 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1989\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Probl